  Act as an ontology engineer. Use the following content (examples, part of the ontology, and a list of guidelines) as a guide to translate the natural language rule you are given into a SWRL rule. 
  EXAMPLES
    Example 1
    Rule in natural language: If a person has a sibling who is a man, then the person has a brother.
    SWRL rule: Person(?p) ^ hasSibling(?p, ?s) ^ Person(?s) ^ IsMan(?s, true) -> hasBrother(?p, ?s)

    Example 2
    Rule in natural language: if a person has a phone number that starts with '+', then the person has an international phone number.
    SWRL rule: Person(?p) ^ hasPhoneNumber(?p, ?number) ^ swrlb:startsWith(?number, "+") -> hasInternationalPhoneNumber(?p, true)

    Example 3
    Rule in natural language:  if a person has age greater than 17, then the person is an adult and has id card.
    SWRL rule: Person(?p) ^ hasAge(?p, ?age) ^ Age(?age) ^ swrlb:greaterThan(?age, 17) ^ IdCard(?id) -> Adult(?p) ^ hasIdCard(?p, ?id)

    Example 4
    Rule in natural language: if a publication has two different authors, then those authors have cooperated with each other.
    SWRL rule: Publication(?p) ^ Author(?y) ^ Author(?z) ^ hasAuthor(?p, ?y) ^ hasAuthor(?p, ?z) ^ differentFrom(?y, ?z) -> cooperatedWith(?y, ?z)

    Example 5
    Rule in natural language: if a researcher has published more than 10 papers in a Top-Tier conference, then the researcher is a prominent researcher and has a high citation impact.
    SWRL rule: Researcher(?r) ^ hasPublished(?r, ?c) ^ Conference(?c) ^ topTierConference(?c) ^ swrlb:greaterThan(count(?c), 10) -> ProminentResearcher(?r) ^ hasHighCitationImpact(?r, true)
  END OF EXAMPLES
  PART OF ONTOLOGY 
    ###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasIncidentSeverity
beAWARE_ontology:hasIncidentSeverity rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                     rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                     rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                     rdfs:label "has incident severity" ;
                                     skos:definition "Indicates the severity of the incident." ;
                                     skos:example "Incidents involving injured or dead people are of high severity." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#detectsIncident
beAWARE_ontology:detectsIncident rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 owl:inverseOf beAWARE_ontology:incidentDetectedBy ;
                                 rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Detection ;
                                 rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                 rdfs:label "detects incident" ;
                                 skos:definition "Indicates which incidents were detected by a specific detection activity." ;
                                 skos:example "A flooding incident, a blocked road etc." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasIncidentPriority
beAWARE_ontology:hasIncidentPriority rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                     rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                     rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                     rdfs:label "has incident priority" ;
                                     skos:definition "Indicates the priority of the incident." ;
                                     skos:example "Incidents involving humans in danger are of high priority." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasDetectionEnd
beAWARE_ontology:hasDetectionEnd rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                 rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Detection ;
                                 rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                 rdfs:label "has detection end" ;
                                 skos:definition "Indicates the end of the detection." .


###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasDetectionRisk
beAWARE_ontology:hasDetectionRisk rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Detection ;
                                  rdfs:range xsd:float ;
                                  rdfs:label "has detection risk" ;
                                  skos:definition "Indicates the risk level of the detection." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#incidentDetectedBy
beAWARE_ontology:incidentDetectedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                    rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:Detection ;
                                    rdfs:label "incident detected by" ;
                                    skos:definition "Indicates the detection activity that detected this incident." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasDetectionStart
beAWARE_ontology:hasDetectionStart rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                   rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Detection ;
                                   rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                   rdfs:label "has detection start" ;
                                   skos:definition "Indicates the start of the detection." .


###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasDetectionTimestamp
beAWARE_ontology:hasDetectionTimestamp rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                       rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Detection ;
                                       rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
                                       rdfs:label "has detection timestamp" ;
                                       skos:definition "Represents the timestamp of the detection." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#involvesIncident
beAWARE_ontology:involvesIncident rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                  rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Dataset ;
                                  rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                  rdfs:label "involves incident" ;
                                  skos:definition "Certain analysis components recognize the major incident (e.g. fire, flood, etc.) portrayed in a media item." .
  END OF ONTOLOGY

  COMMON GUIDELINES

  Please try to implement the following guidelines:
  1: Variables e.g., (?something) used in Conclusions must be present in Conditions. So create as many variables as needed in Conditions. 
  2: Each atom must have exactly one variable if it represents class.
  3: Each atom must have exactly two variables if it represents object property.
  4: Each concept must be represented by a class and must be present in Conditions.

  END OF COMMON GUIDELINES

  The rule in natural language is the following: If a detection has a start time and an end time, and its total duration is calculated to be greater than 60 minutes, then the severity of the incident is 'high'.
